WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:06.621
Journey six: message a business. A member and a business hold a private

00:00:06.621 --> 00:00:11.666
conversation from an inbox. This run finishes what was left.

00:00:12.548 --> 00:00:15.433
On a listing, Message opens a dialog.

00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:20.968
Its hint now names the owner. Typing stops at four thousand characters,

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:24.476
and a counter shows for the last two hundred.

00:00:25.184 --> 00:00:28.363
Once sent, the conversation opens up.

00:00:28.363 --> 00:00:31.543
A toast names the day Trevor is back.

00:00:31.543 --> 00:00:34.808
A line above the messages says it too.

00:00:35.921 --> 00:00:39.809
A long inbox now loads fifty conversations at a time.

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:44.872
The count is of the whole inbox, and Show more conversations adds the

00:00:44.872 --> 00:00:47.513
rest below, by keyboard or by touch.

00:00:48.702 --> 00:00:52.808
A photo is now scanned for malware before it is stored.

00:00:52.808 --> 00:00:57.958
When the scan cannot be done, nothing is stored, and the message says

00:00:57.958 --> 00:00:58.182
so.

00:00:58.889 --> 00:01:03.841
Try again uploads the photo once the scanner answers, and the message is

00:01:03.841 --> 00:01:04.529
sent once.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.559
Behind the screen, the server gives each photo to a ClamAV scanner, and

00:01:10.559 --> 00:01:14.773
only then keeps it in the media store under a random name.

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:17.534
With no scanner, no photo is accepted.

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:21.240
The tests prove it with a stand-in for the scanner.

00:01:22.101 --> 00:01:25.299
Journey six stands at ninety-eight percent.

00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:30.578
What is left is the owner's: a running scanner in Azure, and a separate

00:01:30.578 --> 00:01:31.917
domain for photos.
